p(25,14,"He hung my rein on one of the iron spikes",
 "A colt bumps Lizzie and a boy cracks a whip. Lizzie kicks and runs off wildly with Lady Anne. Black Auster neighs for help, and Blantyre comes running and rides after them.",
 "Blantyre hung my rein on one of the iron spikes and was soon out of sight among the trees. Lizzie was standing quietly at the side of the road a few steps away, with her back to me. My young mistress was sitting easily with a loose rein, singing a little song under her breath. I listened to my rider’s steps until they reached the house, and I heard him knock at the door. There was a field on the other side of the road, and its gate stood open. Just then some cart horses and several young colts came trotting out in a very wild way, with a boy behind them cracking a big whip. The colts were wild and playful, and one of them ran across the road and bumped into Lizzie’s back legs. I cannot say whether it was the stupid colt, or the loud cracking of the whip, or both together, but she gave a hard kick and ran off at a wild gallop. It was so sudden that Lady Anne was nearly thrown off, but she soon got her balance back. I gave a loud, high neigh for help. Again and again I neighed, hitting the ground with my foot in my hurry, and tossing my head to get the rein loose. I did not have to wait long. Blantyre came running to the gate. He looked about in fear and just saw the flying shape, now far away on the road. In a moment he jumped into the saddle. I needed no whip and no spur, because I was as eager as my rider. He saw it, and gave me a free rein, and leaned a little forward, and we raced after them.",
 ["spikes","frolicsome","bolted","blundered","hind","headlong","unseated","shrill","pawing","eager"])
s(25,"I needed no whip, no spur, for I was as eager as my rider",
 "I did not need a whip or a spur, because I wanted to go as much as my rider did.",
 "'as eager as my rider' compares two things that are equal with 'as ... as'; 'no whip, no spur' uses 'no' twice to stress that neither was needed.")
